  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Add `fresh local`, a foreground localhost playground in the repository-built CLI that starts the real login service, securely consumes bootstrap access, provisions a passwordless test account, and opens guided passkey enrollment on first use.\n- Persist private playground state beneath the current user's local application-data directory so later runs immediately exercise passkey sign-in and restart durability; add explicit enrollment recovery, exact alternate-port origins, browser-launch fallback, concurrent-run locking, confirmed reset, and actionable port-conflict handling.\n- Keep the playground loopback-only and isolated from production configuration, cached CLI connections, Docker, and source-tree data; transfer its single-use enrollment credential in a client-only URL fragment that is prefilled and removed before the WebAuthn user gesture.\n- Extract the existing service composition into a reusable login-host boundary while retaining the standalone service entry point, and bundle the login assembly and browser assets into the published CLI directory.\n- Expand CLI, host, storage, lifecycle, redaction, recovery, and package-layout coverage to 491 tests; dogfood guided enrollment, explicit passkey sign-in, mobile/desktop layout, and sign-in after a server restart with headless Playwright and a virtual authenticator.",
